      )SIC

      ⍝ Bugs28 #41 regression: A⍟B with a negative real base was
      ⍝ DOMAIN ERROR as soon as either cell was complex-TYPED, even
      ⍝ though the same base/argument pair as plain real/FloatCells
      ⍝ (¯2⍟8) already gave a well-defined, finite complex result.
      ⍝ Root cause: ComplexCell::bif_logarithm_cc()'s "real base"
      ⍝ shortcut computed log(b)/log(a.real()) using the REAL log(),
      ⍝ which is NaN for a negative a.real() -- rejected by the
      ⍝ isfinite() check right after. Fixed by using the COMPLEX
      ⍝ log(APL_Complex(a.real(),0.0)) instead, taking the
      ⍝ negative-real branch cut correctly (the same way the general,
      ⍝ genuinely-complex-base case just below already does).
      ⍝
